---
description: Never push commits or branches to git remotes unless the user explicitly asks
alwaysApply: true
---

# Git push

- **Never** run `git push`, `git push --force`, or any remote-updating git command unless the user explicitly asks to push in that message.
- Commits are only when the user asks; push is a separate, explicit request.
- If work needs to be on the remote, prepare the commit locally (when asked) and tell the user to push, or wait for them to say "push".
- Do not push "to help" after a fix, deploy prep, or cron change.
